# Introducing Localize

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:localize, "~> 1.0"},
  {:calendrical, "~> 1.0"}
])
```

## Localize 1.0

<!-- slide: logo https://raw.githubusercontent.com/elixir-localize/localize/refs/heads/main/logo.png -->

<!-- slide: author Kip Cole -->

<!-- slide: byline Author of localize, elixir Unicode, Image, Text, ... -->

<!-- slide: event Sydney Elixir Meetup -->

<!-- slide: date 19 August 2026 -->

* Built on over 10 years of ex_cldr (May 2016, 1,970 commits)
* Third major release
  * The very forgettable 1.x chain
  * The not too bad 2.x release chain of the last few years
  * The significantly improved 3.x, known as Localize

## Localize compared to ex_cldr

* No "backend" architecture
* Faster. Often a lot faster.
* Simplified packaging, `Localize`and `Calendrical` replace almost all of the more than 20 `ex_cldr` libraries
* More consistent API naming of functions and arguments
* Better and more complete documentation including guides
* Conforms more closely to TR35
* Includes a full Elixir-native Localized collation
* Includes Message Format 2 (MF2) formatting
* Straight forward migration (according to adopters)

## Performance Comparison

| Area                    | Headline                                                     | Localize advantage            |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------- |
| Compile (per-project)   | Bench.Cldr backend recompile vs Localize touch-and-recompile | **~7× faster** (7 s → 1 s) |
| Number formatting       | Integers, decimals, percent, grouped                         | **~2.5–3.8×**              |
| Currency formatting     | USD in `:en`, `:de`, `:ja`                                   | **~1.8–3.7×**              |
| Date formatting         | Short / medium / long in 3 locales                           | **~2.2–3.1×**              |
| **Time formatting**     | Short / medium in 3 locales                                  | **~15–19×**                |
| **DateTime formatting** | Short / medium / long in 3 locales                           | **~7.4–9.5×**              |
| Unit formatting (long)  | length, mass, temperature                                    | **~1.9–2.7×**              |
| Unit formatting (short) | length, mass, temperature                                    | **~1.8–2.6×**              |
| Memory per call         | Numbers                                                      | **~3–4×** less             |
| Memory per call         | Time / DateTime                                              | **~7–10×** less            |

